nNow `_initialize_geo_bypass({'countries': ['LT']})` \u2014 the real implementation. Let me recall youtube_dl's:\n\n```python\n    def _initialize_geo_bypass(self, geo_bypass_context, countries=None):\n        \"\"\"\n        Initialize geo bypass mechanism using the proxy specified by\n        --geo-bypass-proxy. If geo_bypass_context is a dict and contains\n        a 'countries' key, it will be used to calculate the correct country code,\n        otherwise countries argument will be used if not None.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not self._downloader.params.get('geo_bypass', True):\n            return\n\n        if self._downloader.params.get('geo_bypass_country', None) is not None:\n            self._geo_bypass_country = self._downloader.params.get('geo_bypass_country')\n            self.to_screen('Forcing geo-bypass country: %s' % self._geo_bypass_country)\n            return\n\n        if self._downloader.params.get('geo_bypass_ip_block', None) is not None:\n            self._geo_bypass_ip_block = self._downloader.params.get('geo_bypass_ip_block')\n            self.to_screen('Forcing geo-bypass IP block: %s' % self._geo_bypass_ip_block)\n            return\n\n        if geo_bypass_context is not None and isinstance(geo_bypass_context, dict):\n            countries = geo_bypass_context.get('countries')\n\n        if countries:\n            self._geo_bypass_country = countries[0].upper()  # ??\n```\n\nHmm no. I think it uses `self._X_FF_HEADERS`... Actually I remember:\n\n```python\n        if countries:\n            self._geo_bypass_country = random.choice(countries)  # no...\n```\n\nHmm. Let me think again. The geo bypass in youtube_dl works by setting X-Forwarded-For header with a random IP from the country's IP block. The implementation:\n\n```python\n    def _initialize_geo_bypass(self, geo_bypass_context, countries=None):\n        ...\n        if geo_bypass_context is not None and isinstance(geo_bypass_context, dict):\n            countries = geo_bypass_context.get('countries')\n        if countries:\n            self._geo_bypass_country = countries[0]  # ??\n```\n\nI genuinely don't remember. It might call `self._downloader.params['geo_bypass_proxy']`... Let me just check with get_info. If it's complex/network-free, use real; otherwise monkeypatch with a spy.\n\nActually, you know, I recall now:\n\n```python\n    def _initialize_geo_bypass(self, geo_bypass_context, countries=None):\n        \"\"\"\n        Initialize geo bypass mechanism using the proxy specified by\n        --geo-bypass-proxy. If geo_bypass_context is a dict and contains\n        a 'countries' key, it will be used to calculate the correct country code,\n        otherwise countries argument will be used if not None.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not self._downloader.params.get('geo_bypass', True):\n            return\n\n        if self._downloader.params.get('geo_bypass_country', None) is not None:\n            self._geo_bypass_country = self._downloader.params.get('geo_bypass_country')\n            self.to_screen('Forcing geo-bypass country: %s' % self._geo_bypass_country)\n            return\n\n        if self._downloader.params.get('geo_bypass_ip_block', None) is not None:\n            self._geo_bypass_ip_block = self._downloader.params.get('geo_bypass_ip_block')\n            self.to_screen('Forcing geo-bypass IP block: %s' % self._geo_bypass_ip_block)\n            return\n\n        if geo_bypass_context is not None and isinstance(geo_bypass_context, dict):\n            countries = geo_bypass_context.get('countries')\n\n        if countries:\n            self._geo_bypass_country = countries[0].upper()\n            self.to_screen('Bypassing geo-restriction for country: %s' % self._geo_bypass_country)\n```\n\nHmm, something like that. It's plausible. With FakeDownloader params={}, it would proceed to the countries branch and set `self._geo_bypass_country = 'LT'`. Then we can assert `ie._geo_bypass_country == 'LT'`. That would be a nice postcondition! But I need to verify the actual implementation.\n\nOK, let me now do the get_info calls. I'll batch them:\n\n1. `TVPlayIE`\n2. `InfoExtractor.__init__`\n3. `InfoExtractor._initialize_geo_bypass`\n4. `InfoExtractor.raise_geo_restricted`\n5. `InfoExtractor._sort_formats`\n6. `InfoExtractor._match_id`\n7. `InfoExtractor._parse_json`\n8. `InfoExtractor.to_screen`\n9. `ExtractorError`\n10. `GeoRestrictedError`\n\nThat's a lot; maybe I don't need all. Let me prioritize: TVPlayIE (for _VALID_URL), _initialize_geo_bypass, raise_geo_restricted, _sort_formats, ExtractorError, GeoRestrictedError. And maybe InfoExtractor.__init__ and to_screen.\n\nLet me make the calls now.\n\nAfter getting info, I'll write the test file.\n\nDraft test file:\n\n```python\n# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-\nimport io\n\nimport pytest\n\nfrom youtube_dl.compat import compat_HTTPError\nfrom youtube_dl.extractor.tvplay import TVPlayIE\nfrom youtube_dl.utils import ExtractorError, GeoRestrictedError, parse_iso8601\n\n\nclass FakeDownloader(object):\n    \"\"\"Minimal stand-in for YoutubeDL: only what InfoExtractor touches.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, params=None):\n        self.params = params if params is not None else {}\n\n    def to_screen(self, msg, skip_eol=False):\n        pass\n\n\ndef make_ie(params=None):\n    return TVPlayIE(FakeDownloader(params))\n\n\nVIDEO_URL = 'http://play.tv3.lt/1875169/some-episode'\n\n\ndef make_video_json(**overrides):\n    video = {\n        'title': 'Test Episode',\n        'description': 'Test description',\n        'sami_path': 'http://media.example.com/subs_fi.xml',\n        'format_title': 'Test Series',\n        'format_position': {'episode': 3, 'season': 2},\n        '_embedded': {'season': {'title': 'Season Two'}},\n        'duration': 120,\n        'created_at': '2015-01-02T03:04:05+00:00',\n        'views': {'total': 12345},\n        'age_limit': 16,\n        'is_geo_blocked': False,\n    }\n    video.update(overrides)\n    return video\n\n\ndef install_stream_downloader(monkeypatch, ie, video_json, streams_json):\n    calls = []\n\n    def fake_download_json(url, video_id, note=None, **kwargs):\n        calls.append(url)\n        if '/stream/' in url:\n            return streams_json\n        return video_json\n\n    monkeypatch.setattr(ie, '_download_json', fake_download_json)\n    return calls\n\n\ndef install_format_extractors(monkeypatch, ie):\n    f4m_calls = []\n    m3u8_calls = []\n\n    def fake_f4m(url, video_id, f4m_id=None, fatal=False, **kwargs):\n        f4m_calls.append({'url': url, 'video_id': video_id, 'f4m_id': f4m_id, 'fatal': fatal})\n        return [{'format_id': '%s_fake' % f4m_id, 'url': url, 'ext': 'flv'}]\n\n    def fake_m3u8(url, video_id, ext=None, protocol=None, m3u8_id=None, fatal=False, **kwargs):\n        m3u8_calls.append({'url': url, 'video_id': video_id, 'ext': ext,\n                           'protocol': protocol, 'm3u8_id': m3u8_id, 'fatal': fatal})\n        return [{'format_id': '%s_fake' % m3u8_id, 'url': url, 'ext': ext}]\n\n    monkeypatch.setattr(ie, '_extract_f4m_formats', fake_f4m)\n    monkeypatch.setattr(ie, '_extract_m3u8_formats', fake_m3u8)\n    return f4m_calls, m3u8_calls\n\n\ndef test_full_extraction_all_stream_types(monkeypatch):\n    ie = make_ie()\n    video_json = make_video_json()\n    streams_json = {\n        'streams': {\n            'hls': 'http://hls.example.com/master.m3u8',\n            'hds': 'http://hds.example.com/video.f4m',\n            'medium': 'http://media.example.com/video.mp4',\n            'low': 'rtmp://edge.example.com/liveapp/stream1234',\n            'broken_rtmp': 'rtmp://host-without-app-path',\n            'not_a_url': 12345,\n        }\n    }\n    install_stream_downloader(monkeypatch, ie, video_json, streams_json)\n    f4m_calls, m3u8_calls = install_format_extractors(monkeypatch, ie)\n\n    result = ie._real_extract(VIDEO_URL)\n\n    # Top-level metadata\n    assert result['id'] == '1875169'\n    assert result['title'] == 'Test Episode'\n    assert result['description'] == 'Test description'\n    assert result['series'] == 'Test Series'\n    assert result['episode_number'] == 3\n    assert result['season'] == 'Season Two'\n    assert result['season_number'] == 2\n    assert result['duration'] == 120\n    assert result['timestamp'] == parse_iso8601('2015-01-02T03:04:05+00:00')\n    assert result['view_count'] == 12345\n    assert result['age_limit'] == 16\n\n    # Geo bypass was initialized from the URL TLD\n    assert ie._geo_bypass_country == 'LT'\n\n    # Subtitles from sami_path with embedded language\n    assert result['subtitles'] == {'fi': [{'url': 'http://media.example.com/subs_fi.xml'}]}\n\n    # f4m branch\n    assert len(f4m_calls) == 1\n    assert f4m_calls[0]['url'] == 'http://hds.example.com/video.f4m?hdcore=3.5.0&plugin=aasp-3.5.0.151.81'\n    assert f4m_calls[0]['f4m_id'] == 'hds'\n    assert f4m_calls[0]['fatal'] is False\n\n    # m3u8 branch\n    assert len(m3u8_calls) == 1\n    assert m3u8_calls[0]['url'] == 'http://hls.example.com/master.m3u8'\n    assert m3u8_calls[0]['ext'] == 'mp4'\n    assert m3u8_calls[0]['protocol'] == 'm3u8_native'\n    assert m3u8_calls[0]['m3u8_id'] == 'hls'\n    assert m3u8_calls[0]['fatal'] is False\n\n    formats = result['formats']\n    by_id = {f['format_id']: f for f in formats}\n    # plain http format\n    assert by_id['medium']['url'] == 'http://media.example.com/video.mp4'\n    assert by_id['medium']['ext'] == 'mp4'\n    assert by_id['medium']['quality'] == 1  # qualities(['hls', 'medium', 'high'])\n    # rtmp format split into url/app/play_path\n    assert by_id['low']['ext'] == 'flv'\n    assert by_id['low']['url'] == 'rtmp://edge.example.com/liveapp'\n    assert by_id['low']['app'] == 'liveapp'\n    assert by_id['low']['play_path'] == 'stream1234'\n    assert by_id['low']['preference'] == -1\n    # mocked extractor formats were extended in\n    assert by_id['hds_fake']['url'].startswith('http://hds.example.com/video.f4m')\n    assert by_id['hls_fake']['url'] == 'http://hls.example.com/master.m3u8'\n    # invalid entries were skipped\n    assert 'broken_rtmp' not in by_id\n    assert 'not_a_url' not in by_id\n```\n\nWait \u2014 `by_id` uses format_id keys; the mocked formats have format_id 'hds_fake' and 'hls_fake'. OK.\n\nHmm, one issue: `_sort_formats` real implementation \u2014 will it work with these formats? The formats have 'url', 'ext', 'format_id', 'quality', and for rtmp 'preference'. The real `_sort_formats` in youtube_dl:\n\n```python\n    def _sort_formats(self, formats, field_preference=None):\n        if not formats:\n            raise ExtractorError('No video formats found')\n\n        for f in formats:\n            ...\n```\n\nI need to check. If it requires 'language' or 'url'... Let me check via get_info and adapt. If risky, I'll monkeypatch `_sort_formats` with a spy:\n\n```python\nsort_calls = []\ndef fake_sort(formats, field_preference=None):\n    sort_calls.append(list(formats))\n    formats.sort(key=lambda f: f.get('quality') or 0)\nmonkeypatch.setattr(ie, '_sort_formats', fake_sort)\n```\n\nBut then I can't assert the real sorting happened \u2014 but that's fine, the coverage target is line 303 executing.\n\nHmm, but actually using the real `_sort_formats` is a better test. Let me check its implementation first.\n\nAlso `update_url_query` \u2014 the query param order: `update_url_query(video_url, {'hdcore': '3.5.0', 'plugin': 'aasp-3.5.0.151.81'})` \u2192 'http://hds.example.com/video.f4m?hdcore=3.5.0&plugin=aasp-3.5.0.151.81'. In Python 3.7+, dict order is insertion order, and `update_url_query` uses `compat_parse_qs`/`compat_urllib_parse_urlencode`... The encoded order should follow the dict order. In youtube_dl's update_url_query:\n\n```python\ndef update_url_query(url, query):\n    ...\n    parsed_url = compat_urlparse.urlparse(url)\n    qs = compat_parse_qs(parsed_url.query)\n    qs.update(query)\n    return compat_urlparse.urlunparse(parsed_url._replace(\n        query=compat_urllib_parse_urlencode(qs, True)))\n```\n\n`compat_parse_qs` returns a dict; `qs.update(query)` adds keys; urlencode iterates the dict \u2014 order: existing keys first, then new ones in insertion order ('hdcore', 'plugin'). Since original has no query, order is hdcore, plugin. So the URL is 'http://hds.example.com/video.f4m?hdcore=3.5.0&plugin=aasp-3.5.0.151.81'. \n\nBut to be safe, I could parse the query instead of exact string match:\n\n```python\nfrom youtube_dl.compat import compat_parse_qs, compat_urllib_parse_urlparse\nq = compat_parse_qs(compat_urllib_parse_urlparse(f4m_calls[0]['url']).query)\nassert q.get('hdcore') == ['3.5.0']\nassert q.get('plugin') == ['aasp-3.5.0.151.81']\n```\n\nThat's more robust. youtube_dl.compat has `compat_parse_qs` and `compat_urllib_parse_urlparse`? Let me check: youtube_dl.compat has `compat_parse_qs` (yes) and `compat_urllib_parse_urlparse` (yes, I believe: `compat_urllib_parse_urlparse = urllib.parse.urlparse`). Hmm, in youtube_dl/compat.py:\n\n```python\ntry:\n    import urllib.parse as compat_urllib_parse\nexcept ImportError:\n    import urllib as compat_urllib_parse\n\n...\ncompat_parse_qs = compat_urllib_parse.parse_qs\n...\ncompat_urllib_parse_urlparse = compat_urllib_parse.urlparse\n```\n\nI think `compat_urllib_parse_urlparse` exists. Alternatively just use `urllib.parse` directly in the test (tests run on py3 presumably). Or use `compat_urlparse` \u2014 the snippet imports `from youtube_dl.compat import compat_urlparse`. So `compat_urlparse.urlparse` and `compat_urlparse.parse_qs` exist. I'll use those.\n\nNow the 403 test:\n\n```python\ndef test_403_stream_error_raises_expected_extractor_error(monkeypatch):\n    ie = make_ie()\n    video_json = make_video_json(sami_path=None)\n    error_body = json.dumps({'msg': 'This content is not available in your country'})\n    http_error = compat_HTTPError(\n        'http://playapi.mtgx.tv/v3/videos/stream/1875169', 403, 'Forbidden',\n        {}, io.BytesIO(error_body.enco